Hello Cloudflare team,

Ahead of Web Summit Lisbon, we have written a page about Cloudflare on PrompTugal.news:
https://promptugal.news/companies/cloudflare/

It follows Cloudflare at the summit: "The agentic internet: Who controls the web?", Tuesday 10 November at 11:50.

One section is still empty: Cloudflare's flows, how work moves through your product and where AI agents act in it. We map them only from public pages and never guess, so a few lines from you would get it right faster.

PrompTugal.news is a new newsroom from Portugal, for Europe, with one mandate: to map the universe of AI in Portugal and the companies that come to it. Every fact on the page carries its source and the date we read it; if anything is wrong, reply and we correct it, dated.

The page also asks the three questions we ask every company: what your AI agents can reach, what they are authorised to do, and who controls the gap between the two. Could we hear your answer in 15 minutes during the summit, 9 to 12 November? Answering is optional. If you would rather talk than publish, we can just talk. Reply with a time that suits you.

Best regards,
